<title>JAPAN: Yaohan shares slip as debt worries persist.</title>
<headline>Yaohan shares slip as debt worries persist.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in supermarket chain operator Yaohan Japan Corp slipped on Thursday morning, amid persistent market jitters over the financial health of the retailer as it struggles with heavy debt after aggressive expansion overseas, brokers said.</p>
<p>They noted stop-loss selling of the shares by investors.</p>
<p>As of 0121 GMT, Yaohan's shares were down down 15 yen or 9.38 percent at 145, making it the largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
